    </figure>

    <!-- Editorial Prose -->
        <!-- GEO & AEO Key Takeaways Box (BLUF) -->
    <aside class="ai-quick-summary-card" aria-label="Gladiator 2 Filming Locations Morocco Quick Answer">
      <div class="ai-summary-header">
        <span class="ai-summary-kicker">⚡ QUICK ANSWER: GLADIATOR II FILMING LOCATIONS IN MOROCCO</span>
        <span class="ai-summary-badge">Cinematic Heritage</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ai-summary-text">
        Director Ridley Scott filmed <em>Gladiator II</em> (and the original 2000 <em>Gladiator</em>) predominantly in <strong>Ouarzazate</strong> and the UNESCO World Heritage ksar of <strong>Aït Benhaddou</strong> in southern Morocco. Key production sites include the ancient clay arena sets inside Aït Benhaddou and the massive Colosseum replica built in the desert plains outside <strong>CLA and Atlas Film Studios</strong>, easily visited on a private day trip from Marrakech.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <div class="article-content">

      <!-- AEO Quick Answer Snapshot -->
      <div style="background: #ffffff; border-left: 4px solid var(--gold, #C8A45C); border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12); border-right: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12); padding: 24px 28px; margin-bottom: 36px; box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
        <strong style="display: block; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #000000; margin-bottom: 8px;">Quick Answer: Where Was Gladiator II Filmed in Morocco?</strong>
        <p style="font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(0,0,0,0.85); margin: 0;">
          Ridley Scott chose the fortified desert city of <strong>Ouarzazate</strong> and the UNESCO World Heritage site of <strong>Kasbah Ait Benhaddou</strong> in southern Morocco as the primary filming locations for <em>Gladiator II</em>. Production constructed custom Roman arena sets on the outdoor backlots of <strong>Atlas Film Studios</strong>, returning to the very same red-earthen valley where the original Oscar-winning <em>Gladiator</em> was filmed in 1999.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 1.25rem;">
        When director Ridley Scott envisioned the dusty, sun-bleached Roman gladiator training arena for the original 2000 film <em>Gladiator</em>, he did not build in Rome or Los Angeles. He journeyed to the desert foothills of southern Morocco, where the ancient mud-brick citadel of <strong>Ait Benhaddou</strong> rises majestically from the Ounila River valley.
      </p>

      <p>
        Nearly a quarter-century later, Scott returned to the same storied valley to shoot <em>Gladiator II</em>. For movie lovers, walking through the narrow alleyways of Ait Benhaddou and exploring the colossal soundstages of Ouarzazate is one of the most unforgettable cultural excursions in North Africa.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you are planning your trip, Roam Morocco operates a dedicated, private <a href="/tour-heritage-cinema.html"><strong>Morocco Film Location Tour (Ait Benhaddou &amp; Atlas Studios)</strong></a> with private chauffeur pickup from your Marrakech riad. In this insider guide, we unveil the exact locations where cinema history was made.
      </p>

      <!-- Matrix of Iconic Movies Filmed in Morocco -->
      <h2 id="hollywood-in-the-sahara">Hollywood in the Sahara: Iconic Films Shot in Ouarzazate &amp; Ait Benhaddou</h2>
      <p>
        Ouarzazate has earned its nickname as the <em>"Ouallywood"</em> of Africa. Here is a definitive guide to major blockbusters filmed across these landscapes:
      </p>

      <div class="roam-table-wrapper">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Film / TV Series</th>
              <th>Morocco Filming Site</th>
              <th>Iconic Scene / Depiction</th>
              <th>Visiting Accessibility</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Gladiator II (2024)</strong></td>
              <td>Ait Benhaddou &amp; Atlas Studios Backlot</td>
              <td>Roman arena skirmishes, Numidian outposts, and training grounds</td>
              <td>Open daily; walk the real riverbed and studio sets</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Gladiator (2000)</strong></td>
              <td>Kasbah Ait Benhaddou</td>
